  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The FeSL PEP contains a response cache.  Evaluation requests and responses are cached, so that repeating the same request will result in returning a cached item rather than re-evaluating the request.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Environment variable PEP_NOCACHE can be set to true to completely disable the cache.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Currently when policies are added, edited etc, the cache is not invalidated, with the impact that existing cache entries not reflecting the policy change could be returned (ie incorrect evaluation response).  The default cache expiry time is 10 minutes, so policy changes are not guaranteed completely effective until after this time.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Provide some means of clearing the cache, eg a configurable option so that (optionally) when a policy is added etc the cache is cleared.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
